    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="1092" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg878"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 392.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Mr.
                        Rublee.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 50.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1871-07-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 18, 1871.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I transmit to you herewith the draught of a
                        note,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d414-f1"/> which you will present to the
                    government of the Swiss Confederation, requesting that <pb facs="1093" n="879"
                        xml:id="pg879"/> the President of that confederation will be pleased to
                    appoint an arbitrator to form, with the arbitrators to be named by the President
                    of the United States, by Her Britannic Majesty, and by the Emperor of Brazil,
                    the tribunal of arbitration to which, in pursuance of the first article of the
                    treaty signed at Washington on the 8th of May, of which a copy is sent to you
                    herewith, the United States and Her Britannic Majesty have agreed that all the
                    claims growing out of the acts committed by the several vessels which have given
                    rise to the claims generically known as the “Alabama claims” shall be referred.
                    You will arrange with your British colleague for the simultaneous presentation
                    of your respective notes on this subject. You will not fail to draw the
                    attention of the Swiss minister for foreign affairs unofficially to the last
                    clause of the first article as to the period within which it is hoped that an
                    arbitrator may be named.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
